  "suggestedProse": [
    "Across 32 complete Resource Graph exports retained from October 7 at 20:28 UTC through October 9 at 17:43 UTC, I counted 33 KSPM-Agentless row-sightings, all Unhealthy. These were repeated sightings of two findings, not 33 distinct findings. The set includes two preflight exports. No Healthy row was captured in this sample; that does not establish that this assessment path can never return one.",
    "The old pod reference outlived the pod. An ARM export at 14:21:28 UTC on October 9 still named the pod whose deletion request had been accepted at 13:41:35 UTC the previous day—about 24 hours 40 minutes earlier. The nearest preceding complete ARG export, at 14:15:37 UTC, also retained that reference. These were separate observations, not simultaneous reads or measurements of the backend scan interval.",
    "At the 17:43 Kubernetes capture, the old ReplicaSet still retained readOnlyRootFilesystem: false, but both its desired and actual replica counts were zero and it owned none of the current pods. The active Deployment and both current pods were read-only. I did not delete that rollback history to obtain the observed finding disappearance.",
    "The findings' first-evaluation timestamps were about 6 hours 32 minutes after workload creation. I first captured the findings locally at 13:20 UTC on October 8. The service timestamps and the time I observed the results answer different questions; neither defines a fixed delivery delay."
  ],
